1
00:00:43,220 --> 00:00:46,544
=Born Again=

2
00:00:46,544 --> 00:00:49,547
=Episode 9=

3
00:01:07,240 --> 00:01:08,560
(Among all of them,)

4
00:01:08,560 --> 00:01:10,000
only Xia Na has type O blood.

5
00:01:10,640 --> 00:01:12,440
And she's terrified of needles.

6
00:01:12,440 --> 00:01:14,760
She'll definitely faint
during the blood draw.

7
00:01:15,600 --> 00:01:16,800
And then

8
00:01:16,800 --> 00:01:17,800
you'll have your chance.

9
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:21,160
The Lus are in a rush
for the match results,

10
00:01:22,080 --> 00:01:23,520
so they won't retest.

11
00:01:39,320 --> 00:01:41,160
(Once the results are in,)

12
00:01:41,160 --> 00:01:43,920
(and they realize Xia Na is the match,)

13
00:01:43,920 --> 00:01:46,160
(it's going to be quite a show.)

14
00:01:56,040 --> 00:01:57,920
After searching for so long,

15
00:01:57,920 --> 00:02:00,480
the match is right beside me all along.

16
00:02:02,320 --> 00:02:04,960
What a lucky break!

17
00:02:05,880 --> 00:02:08,360
Oh, Xiaotang...

18
00:02:08,360 --> 00:02:10,640
You really got off easy.

19
00:02:13,040 --> 00:02:15,000
If not for this kidney match,

20
00:02:15,200 --> 00:02:18,400
why would the company
back that useless girl?

21
00:02:19,840 --> 00:02:22,800
It even cost me a lot of effort
to try to marry her.

22
00:02:24,640 --> 00:02:25,640
Very well.

23
00:02:28,320 --> 00:02:30,240
Aren't you two supposed to be besties?

24
00:02:30,640 --> 00:02:32,760
One provides the organ,

25
00:02:33,680 --> 00:02:35,560
and the other makes me money,

26
00:02:36,640 --> 00:02:37,800
each playing her part.

27
00:02:38,080 --> 00:02:39,520
What a perfect arrangement.

28
00:02:41,760 --> 00:02:42,760
Director Zhang,

29
00:02:43,760 --> 00:02:46,280
make sure she settles in here.

30
00:02:46,520 --> 00:02:47,840
Find the right moment,

31
00:02:48,560 --> 00:02:49,560
and get the surgery done.

32
00:02:50,800 --> 00:02:53,720
Mr. Lu, this... this violates protocol!

33
00:02:54,600 --> 00:02:57,040
Without informed consent
from her or her family,

34
00:02:57,040 --> 00:02:58,040
this is illegal.

35
00:02:58,040 --> 00:02:59,040
I could go to prison!

36
00:03:04,520 --> 00:03:08,040
You've taken no small sum from me
over the years, right?

37
00:03:08,960 --> 00:03:13,440
It should be enough to keep you cozy
for the rest of your life behind bars.

38
00:03:16,040 --> 00:03:17,240
Do the job right,

39
00:03:17,680 --> 00:03:20,240
and there'll be plenty more for you.

40
00:03:20,840 --> 00:03:22,640
But if you mess this up...

41
00:03:27,200 --> 00:03:28,200
The director, huh?

42
00:03:29,800 --> 00:03:32,160
I'll ruin you first.

43
00:03:33,080 --> 00:03:34,160
Do you hear me?

44
00:03:59,960 --> 00:04:00,960
It was just an act.

45
00:04:01,200 --> 00:04:02,600
Why hurt yourself so badly?

46
00:04:03,600 --> 00:04:04,760
I'm not afraid to die anyway.

47
00:04:05,480 --> 00:04:08,240
If I die,
I'll just reload and start over.

48
00:04:10,560 --> 00:04:12,560
Come here. Let me change your dressing.

49
00:04:13,200 --> 00:04:14,280
I'm fine. Nothing major.

50
00:04:14,680 --> 00:04:15,680
It'll heal soon.

51
00:04:21,240 --> 00:04:22,240
Really, no need.

52
00:04:24,880 --> 00:04:25,880
Sit still.

53
00:04:27,880 --> 00:04:29,880
You're not even from this hospital,

54
00:04:29,880 --> 00:04:31,040
and you're this attentive.

55
00:04:36,200 --> 00:04:38,800
Do you never smile when you're working?

56
00:04:49,840 --> 00:04:50,840
Can I ask you something?

57
00:04:50,840 --> 00:04:51,840
Go ahead.

58
00:04:52,720 --> 00:04:54,400
With your personality

59
00:04:54,640 --> 00:04:55,640
and your line of work,

60
00:04:56,320 --> 00:04:59,440
dating must be pretty hard, huh?

61
00:04:59,920 --> 00:05:00,920
Never thought about it.

62
00:05:02,400 --> 00:05:03,400
Fine.

63
00:05:05,320 --> 00:05:06,960
So you've never had a real relationship.

64
00:05:07,320 --> 00:05:09,400
But a secret crush...
You must have had one, right?

65
00:05:16,760 --> 00:05:18,880
You're such a closed book.

66
00:05:18,880 --> 00:05:21,880
If you have a crush on someone
and never say it,

67
00:05:21,880 --> 00:05:23,560
they'll never know in this life.

68
00:05:38,160 --> 00:05:40,760
Wait. Do you really
have a crush on someone?

69
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:42,800
Who is she? Do I know her?

70
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:44,000
Is she a classmate of ours?

71
00:05:44,360 --> 00:05:45,360
Come on. Tell me.

72
00:05:45,480 --> 00:05:46,840
No... Nobody.

73
00:05:47,240 --> 00:05:48,520
Stingy.

74
00:05:51,880 --> 00:05:52,880
A crush?

75
00:05:55,280 --> 00:05:56,560
What does that feel like?

76
00:06:04,600 --> 00:06:05,720
Having a crush

77
00:06:06,680 --> 00:06:09,560
is like having
a secret little world of your own.

78
00:06:12,520 --> 00:06:13,960
(Just watching from afar)

79
00:06:15,720 --> 00:06:16,720
(is more than enough.)

80
00:06:24,120 --> 00:06:25,120
I don't get it.

81
00:06:25,560 --> 00:06:26,840
I've never had a crush before.

82
00:06:28,640 --> 00:06:30,280
Then why haven't you told her?

83
00:06:30,760 --> 00:06:31,880
Afraid she'll turn you down?

84
00:06:34,160 --> 00:06:35,160
Yeah.

85
00:06:37,320 --> 00:06:38,320
Don't worry.

86
00:06:38,480 --> 00:06:40,480
If she turns you down,
you can come to me.

87
00:06:42,880 --> 00:06:43,880
Come to you?

88
00:06:46,920 --> 00:06:49,000
I'll drink with you, chat,

89
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:50,240
watch movies, and have BBQ.

90
00:06:50,680 --> 00:06:53,200
We're classmates.
Pretty solid friend, right?

91
00:06:56,080 --> 00:06:58,920
So, do you think I should tell her?

92
00:07:02,680 --> 00:07:03,680
I don't know.

93
00:07:04,840 --> 00:07:07,960
Right now, I can't
give any relationship advice.

94
00:07:08,760 --> 00:07:10,120
I used to believe in love.

95
00:07:11,240 --> 00:07:13,440
But now, I think it's all fake.

96
00:07:13,760 --> 00:07:15,560
If someone told me
they liked me right now,

97
00:07:15,880 --> 00:07:17,200
I definitely wouldn't believe it.

98
00:07:17,720 --> 00:07:19,200
After going through so many loops,

99
00:07:19,200 --> 00:07:20,720
I've seen the world for what it is.

100
00:07:21,160 --> 00:07:24,080
I don't think anyone in this world
is worth my true feelings.

101
00:07:26,200 --> 00:07:27,200
Except for you.

102
00:07:27,600 --> 00:07:30,040
We're best friends and old classmates.

103
00:07:33,800 --> 00:07:34,800
But Ye Shen,

104
00:07:36,360 --> 00:07:37,560
promise me one thing.

105
00:07:37,880 --> 00:07:38,880
What is it?

106
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:40,120
Swear it first.

107
00:07:44,480 --> 00:07:45,480
We'll always

108
00:07:46,840 --> 00:07:48,880
be best friends.

109
00:07:51,080 --> 00:07:52,080
But

110
00:07:52,720 --> 00:07:53,960
if you ever betray me,

111
00:07:54,200 --> 00:07:56,200
you'll end up worse than them.

112
00:07:56,200 --> 00:07:57,200
Got it?

113
00:08:05,240 --> 00:08:06,520
I can hear it.

114
00:08:06,520 --> 00:08:09,560
Your heart's racing.

115
00:08:10,600 --> 00:08:12,960
Ye Shen, since we're at the hospital,

116
00:08:13,680 --> 00:08:14,720
why not get it checked?

117
00:08:22,720 --> 00:08:25,920
Seriously, that heart rate
is definitely abnormal.

118
00:08:25,920 --> 00:08:28,880
You're a doctor.
You should really take care of yourself.

119
00:08:28,880 --> 00:08:30,880
- I'm fine.
- Did you hear me?

120
00:08:30,880 --> 00:08:31,880
I'm really fine.

121
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:45,600
How long are you going to
keep listening?

122
00:08:55,440 --> 00:08:56,440
You're here.

123
00:09:02,280 --> 00:09:05,800
Did I just hear you talking to someone?

124
00:09:08,440 --> 00:09:10,520
The doctor just checked on my recovery.

125
00:09:15,240 --> 00:09:16,240
Really?

126
00:09:17,160 --> 00:09:18,160
Yes.

127
00:09:19,680 --> 00:09:20,760
Thank you, Doctor.

128
00:09:32,560 --> 00:09:33,560
Wait.

129
00:09:44,600 --> 00:09:47,480
I've never seen this doctor before.

130
00:09:47,480 --> 00:09:48,480
Have we met?

131
00:09:50,240 --> 00:09:52,240
(If Ye Shen gets exposed,)

132
00:09:52,240 --> 00:09:54,560
(all our efforts
will go down the drain.)

133
00:09:59,360 --> 00:10:00,440
The hospital is huge.

134
00:10:00,880 --> 00:10:02,640
You can't have met every doctor here.

135
00:10:04,800 --> 00:10:09,440
Actually, my dad brought me here
for meetings since I was a kid.

136
00:10:09,720 --> 00:10:11,920
I know all the doctors.

137
00:10:15,760 --> 00:10:16,760
I...

138
00:10:17,480 --> 00:10:18,520
I'm just an intern.

139
00:10:18,680 --> 00:10:20,760
Is that so?
Which professor do you work under?

140
00:10:25,160 --> 00:10:26,160
Turn around.

141
00:10:37,080 --> 00:10:38,200
Take off your mask.

142
00:10:41,600 --> 00:10:42,600
Take it off!

143
00:10:50,680 --> 00:10:51,680
Hurry up!

144
00:11:26,808 --> 00:11:30,164
♪The face deep in the heart♪

145
00:11:30,356 --> 00:11:32,818
♪Suddenly clear and hazy♪

146
00:11:34,193 --> 00:11:37,893
♪Across time and space, eyes meet again♪

147
00:11:38,104 --> 00:11:40,544
♪Deeply trapped in the vortex♪

148
00:11:40,691 --> 00:11:43,063
♪Searching for familiar outlines♪

149
00:11:43,213 --> 00:11:45,970
♪Persistently guarding,
endlessly cycling♪

150
00:11:45,970 --> 00:11:48,291
♪Even for just a second♪

151
00:11:49,636 --> 00:11:53,099
♪If raindrops flow backward
into the sky♪

152
00:11:53,227 --> 00:11:55,076
♪And sunlight reverses♪

153
00:11:55,076 --> 00:11:58,546
♪As the sun rises and sets,
we reunite with yesterday♪

154
00:11:58,902 --> 00:12:00,976
♪I'll build a dream with you♪

155
00:12:01,478 --> 00:12:04,887
♪Upon the ruins, spring breeze arrives♪

156
00:12:05,144 --> 00:12:10,356
♪Even if there's no end,
I won't regret the start♪

157
00:12:11,610 --> 00:12:14,175
♪Eternity like a day, rushing to you♪

158
00:12:14,217 --> 00:12:17,670
♪You don't need to recognize my eyes♪

159
00:12:18,247 --> 00:12:21,210
♪Following the tracks
of the days that were♪

160
00:12:21,955 --> 00:12:24,563
♪A day like a lifetime, rushing to you♪

161
00:12:24,563 --> 00:12:28,186
♪You don't need to remember my name♪

162
00:12:28,656 --> 00:12:32,712
♪I'll be the dawn you haven't seen♪
